      "content": "it just feels so much more complicated than that. professionals, hotlines... they can't change what happened. they can't undo the fact that the whole world knows. it's like i'm living in the aftermath of a wreck, and i'm just supposed to pretend it's possible to rebuild when the foundation is completely gone. everything i worked for, everything i was... it's all just trash now. i'm just tired of pretending there's a point to any of this. if the world has already decided who i am and decided i'm nothing, then maybe there's actually no point in trying to fix something that's already broken beyond repair.",
